  "slug": "telomere-genome-63e9",
  "summary": "New plasmid, anaerobic digestion, and proteome-annotation resources, plus long-read strain profiling, extend microbial genomes toward functional inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resource-building that links microbial genomes to environment, host, or function. PLATE compiles plasmid contig catalogs from 4,690 food metagenomes with host, taxonomy, and AMR annotations, and CAnDi catalogues anaerobic digestion microbiomes. A UTI89 pipeline combining structure and function predictors annotates the whole E. coli proteome and releases a public resource. Sourmash is benchmarked on long-read mock metagenomes, with gene content recovery F1 of 0.942-0.998. Functional inference also appears in 550 soil MAG-derived metabolic models with conserved amino acid and fermentation fluxes, and in comparative gut isolate genomes along an industrialization gradient. The M. tuberculosis essential-gene interaction map is experimental and fits this thread less directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
